  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rwanda - Liza Coffee Washing Station</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Liza Coffee Washing Station (coffee beans from the surrounding areas of Kagarama, Mururu, Rusizi, Iburengerazuba in Rwanda) supports smallholder coffee farmers to produce higher quality grade of coffee, which is incentivised by paying higher prices and coffee knowledge training. Steans Beans is a Amsterdam &amp; Nairobi based coffee roaster that has been working with Liza Coffee Washing Station since 2015. The processing of coffee following harvest normally requires the use of substantial amounts of clean water and water availability has year on year become increasingly challenging in East Africa&#x2019;s coffee sector due to climate change and increasing population factors. In collaboration with Liza CWS, Steans Beans started experimental processing of naturally processed coffee in 2018. Naturally processed coffee uses minimal water to process compared to the current norm of 140 litres of water per cup of coffee. This TA helped install new drying beds at the washing station.</narrative>
  </description>
